{
 "version": 1,
 "doc": "ITR Showcase loot manifest. Custom loot tags with tiered budgets (never the vanilla zone tags, whose budgets are save-wide) and custom generator IDs. The loader reads it at startup and adds each tag to the game config's LootArray (TMap add: key = tag, LootTable = the stock DataTable of source_tag, whose used points are shared with that zone; LootPoints = loot_points). While the map is loaded, the loader points each entry at the map's DataTable named by table_name / table_asset (held by BP_ItrShowcase_LootTables), and back at the stock table when the map goes.",
 "budget_rule": "loot_points = max(1, round(source_zone_budget * scale)); source_zone_budget = sum of the source zone's area tags of that category (e.g. Buffer Ammo = BlockPost 24 + CarDepot 20 + TrainStation 32); scale = the tier's footprint in hectares / the source zone's footprint in hectares. Stash.* tags are zone-wide in 2.7.2 and scale the same way; a stash tag's budget is never below the points of the stash nodes placed on it.",
